 "conclusion": "On 15,202 cells, 968 prompts and 1011 raters -- the full population entries 21/22 were measured on -- with demographics at 100% coverage across six axes and 47 group cells: 30 cells cleared the pre-registered floor of 20 raters and 17 did not. The estimand is the DEPARTURE from the arithmetic line, beta_d - k*beta_sum with k=0.26514, because entry 24 established that beta_d itself is the line: any covariate raising both arms yields a differential proportional to their accuracy gap. Largest |t| among tested cells is 1.83; after Benjamini-Hochberg at q=0.05, 0 cells survive. The positive control plants a one-armed group effect and recovers it at retention 89.9% with t 4.89 for g=0.02, so a null here is a measurement rather than silence. The negative control is NOT a permutation -- 200 synthetic groups matched on size and mean own-error give a 95% band of [-0.00814,+0.00697], so a group differing only in noisiness lands on the line. WORLD: W-ANONYMOUS. No demographic group departs from the arithmetic line, on the only release carrying both the compilation contrast and the demographics. The rater component of entries 21/22 is real and ANONYMOUS. 'Identifiable subgroup' leaves the claim permanently and is not to be reopened on another dataset.",
